---
title: The Envelope — Trigger & fulfilment (mail path)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SCH as Scheduler
    participant WK as Dispatch worker
    participant DB as Supabase
    participant P as Pingen API
    participant OP as Operator alert

    SCH->>WK: invoke daily 08:00 CET (shared-secret header)
    WK->>DB: UPDATE cron_heartbeat SET last_run_at = now()

    WK->>DB: SELECT id FROM letters WHERE deliver_on <= current_date AND status = 'scheduled' FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
    Note over WK,DB: `<=` not `=` — a missed run self-catches-up.

    loop each due letter
        WK->>DB: UPDATE letters SET status='sending' WHERE id=$1 AND status='scheduled' RETURNING *
        alt CAS won
            DB-->>WK: row
            WK->>WK: decrypt via keyring[key_version]
            WK->>P: POST letters.create (idempotency key = letter id)
            alt success
                P-->>WK: pingen_id
                WK->>DB: status='sent', pingen_id, sent_at=now()
            else failure
                P-->>WK: error
                WK->>DB: status='retry', attempts = attempts + 1
                WK->>OP: alert — send failed
            end
        else CAS lost
            DB-->>WK: no row — another run claimed it, never double-mail
        end
    end

    WK->>DB: SELECT count(*) FROM letters WHERE deliver_on < current_date - 1 AND status IN ('scheduled','retry')
    alt overdue backlog present
        WK->>OP: alert — letters overdue, scheduler may be dead
    end

    Note over SCH,OP: Watchdog: an external check on cron_heartbeat.last_run_at<br/>catches the case where the scheduler stops firing entirely.
